Subject: tooltip-v2: a closed tooltip is only its trigger element until a pointer reaches it

What: TooltipV2 draws its trigger div with the attributes Kobalte gives a closed trigger
(data-closed, no aria-describedby) and mounts Kobalte's tooltip, its trigger handlers
and the expanded-child observer on the first pointerenter or the first forceOpen, and
keeps them mounted from then on, so a forced open closes through Kobalte as before.
Kobalte's trigger is spread onto that same div through adoptElement (a new
adopt-element.ts, shared with menu-v2), so the children are never re-created, and the
pointerenter is replayed so Kobalte's open delay starts as before. The pointerdown and
keydown "capture" props are dropped: Solid bound them as listeners for events named
pointerdowncapture and keydowncapture, which never fire.
Why: every tooltip in a transcript row and the composer built Kobalte's tooltip state
and five trigger listeners at mount, whether or not a pointer ever reached it.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/adopt-element.ts b/src/v2/components/adopt-element.ts
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..43bc7ecd8d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/v2/components/adopt-element.ts
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+import { splitProps } from "solid-js"
+import { spread } from "solid-js/web"
+
+/**
+ * A Kobalte part given this as its `as` renders onto an element that is
+ * already drawn, so that element's children are never re-created and focus
+ * inside them survives.
+ */
+export function adoptElement(target: () => HTMLElement | undefined) {
+  return (props: Record<string, unknown>) => {
+    const [, rest] = splitProps(props, ["children", "as"])
+    const node = target()
+    if (node) spread(node, rest, false, true)
+    return undefined
+  }
+}
